  "worked_solution": "Since we have that \n\n$$\nP(x)\u21d4Q(x)\u2261(P(x)\u2227Q(x))\u2228(\u00acP(x)\u2227\u00acQ(x)),\n$$\n\n \n\nthe corresponding truth set can be found as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}_{P\u21d4Q}=({T}_{P}\\cap {T}_{Q})\\cup ({\\overset{\u2015}{T}}_{P}\\cap {\\overset{\u2015}{T}}_{Q})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we sketch the set ${T}_{P}\\cap {T}_{Q}:$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14099768/assets/e995ce9652d431c39c7a629a5e825c91fcdb2da56b83ad371c6bb319bc548eb9.png)\n\nThen, we sketch the set ${\\overset{\u2015}{T}}_{P}$ and ${\\overset{\u2015}{T}}_{Q}:$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14099768/assets/fa491500bff1c1e9d0f8453552f33b8deed066e3799a36817d039fc625eee47d.png)\n\nAs a result, ${\\overset{\u2015}{T}}_{P}\\cap {\\overset{\u2015}{T}}_{Q}$ is the following: \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14099768/assets/fbcbb5ebd87fef90163ce5a358beb7bc40b4c4b3d91b89684500577ccedf2b13.png)\n\nFinally, to get the truth set of $P(x)\u21d4Q(x),$ we take all the points that belong to ${T}_{P}\\cap {T}_{Q}$ or ${\\overset{\u2015}{T}}_{P}\\cap {\\overset{\u2015}{T}}_{Q}:$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14099768/assets/01776646145493da01e17a764ee1b71161595bcc249f376fc18cd9325a8218e7.png)",
